// result_end

\caption(The 16 nonlinear activations on minus 4 to 4, in four families. Top left: ReLU, leaky ReLU with slope 0.2, ELU and SELU. Top right: GELU, SiLU, Mish and softplus. Bottom left: sigmoid, tanh, softsign and log-sigmoid. Bottom right: ReLU6, hard sigmoid, hard swish and hard tanh.)
\alttext(Top left: four rectifiers coincide for positive x, SELU slightly steeper; for negative x ReLU is 0, leaky ReLU falls linearly to minus 0.8, ELU flattens towards minus 1 and SELU towards minus 1.76. Top right: GELU, SiLU and Mish dip slightly below 0 near x equals minus 1 and approach the line y equals x for large x; softplus stays positive, from near 0 to about 4. Bottom left: sigmoid rises from 0 to 1, tanh and softsign from minus 1 to 1, softsign more gradually, and log-sigmoid rises from minus 4 to 0. Bottom right: ReLU6 equals x on 0 to 4; hard sigmoid is a ramp from 0 at minus 3 to 1 at 3; hard swish dips to minus 0.375 at minus 1.5 and joins y equals x at 3; hard tanh is flat at minus 1, a ramp from minus 1 to 1, then flat at 1.)

Every activation agrees with its closed form to within \(9\times10^{-16}\), and every autograd derivative to within \(4.4\times10^{-16}\), a few units in the last place of float64. The grid values reproduce the
original example's table. At the kinks the gradient takes one side's value: ReLU's and ReLU6's derivatives are 0 at 0, ReLU6's is 0 at 6, hard tanh's is 1 at \(\pm1\), and hard swish's is 0 at \(-3\) and 1 at 3. SELU's derivative at 0
is \(\lambda\), the right-hand slope. None of this matters for training, since a kink is hit with probability zero.

GELU, SiLU, Mish and hard swish dip to minima of \(-0.170\), \(-0.2785\), \(-0.309\) and \(-0.375\). SiLU's has a closed form. Setting \(f'=\sigma(x)(1+x(1-\sigma(x)))\) to zero gives \(\sigma(x^\ast)=(1+x^\ast)/x^\ast\),
so \(f(x^\ast)=x^\ast\sigma(x^\ast)=1+x^\ast\). The solution is \(x^\ast=-1-W(1/e)=-1.2785\) with Lambert's \(W\) (Corless et al., 1996), and the bisection finds \(x^\ast=-1.2785\), \(f=-0.2785\). The four gated units halve the
last axis (\([5,8]\to[5,4]\)) and pass both finite-difference checks, with largest first-derivative error \(1.7\times10^{-10}\).

> Checking the theory

>> Moments, gains and SELU

The next program tabulates `nn::activation_moments` for every activation at \(q=1\), solves SELU's two equations, iterates SELU's variance map and the gated map, and compares 30-layer networks of width 256 with their mean-field predictions.
The networks use LeCun-normal weights (\(s=1\)), a batch of 256 standard-normal inputs and `nn::init::signal_propagation`.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/activations_depth.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

namespace nn = dm::nn;
using nn::Activation;

int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  // Gaussian moments of every activation at q = 1, and the weight scale that makes q = 1 a fixed point.
  std::print("| activation | E f(Z) | Var f(Z) | E f(Z)² | E f′(Z) | E f′(Z)² | gain √(1/E f²) | χ at that gain |\n");
  std::print("| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for (int k = 1; k <= static_cast<int>(nn::kLastActivation); ++k) {
    const auto a = static_cast<Activation>(k);
    const auto m = nn::activation_moments(a);
    std::print("| {} | {:.4f} | {:.4f} | {:.4f} | {:.4f} | {:.4f} | {:.4f} | {:.4f} |\n", nn::activation_name(a), m.mean,
               m.variance, m.second_moment, m.derivative_mean, m.derivative_second_moment, 1 / std::sqrt(m.second_moment),
               m.derivative_second_moment / m.second_moment);
  }
  std::print("\nPyTorch gains: relu {:.4f}, tanh {:.4f}, selu {:.4f}, leaky_relu(0.2) {:.4f}.\n", nn::init::gain("relu"),
             nn::init::gain("tanh"), nn::init::gain("selu"), nn::init::gain("leaky_relu", 0.2));

  // SELU's constants in closed form: mean 0 and second moment 1 under N(0, 1).
  const double phi0 = 1 / std::sqrt(2 * std::numbers::pi);
  auto Phi = [](double x) { return 0.5 * std::erfc(-x / std::sqrt(2.0)); };
  const double m1 = std::exp(0.5) * Phi(-1) - 0.5;                                    // E[(e^Z - 1) 1{Z<0}]
  const double m2 = std::exp(2.0) * Phi(-2) - 2 * std::exp(0.5) * Phi(-1) + 0.5;      // E[(e^Z - 1)^2 1{Z<0}]
  const double alpha = -phi0 / m1, lambda = 1 / std::sqrt(0.5 + alpha * alpha * m2);
  std::print("\nSELU from the two moment equations: alpha = {:.16f}, lambda = {:.16f}.\n", alpha, lambda);
  std::print("Library constants:                  alpha = 1.6732632423543772, lambda = 1.0507009873554805.\n");
  const auto ms = nn::activation_moments(Activation::Selu);
  std::print("Quadrature check: E selu(Z) = {:.1e}, E selu(Z)² = {:.8f}, chi = E selu′(Z)² = {:.4f}.\n", ms.mean,
             ms.second_moment, ms.derivative_second_moment);
  // The (mean, variance) fixed point is attracting: iterate the map from a perturbed start.
  std::print("SELU variance map from q = 0.25 and q = 4: ");
  for (double q0 : {0.25, 4.0}) {
    double q = q0;
    std::print("{}", q0);
    for (int l = 0; l < 6; ++l) { q = nn::activation_moments(Activation::Selu, q).second_moment; std::print(" → {:.4f}", q); }
    std::print(";  ");
  }
  std::print("\n");

  // A gated unit a * silu(b) with a, b ~ N(0, q) independent: q -> s q E silu(sqrt(q) Z)^2, s = 1 / E silu(Z)^2.
  const double sg = 1 / nn::activation_moments(Activation::Silu).second_moment;
  auto gated = [sg](double q) { return sg * q * nn::activation_moments(Activation::Silu, q).second_moment; };
  const double e = 1e-4;
  std::print("Gated (SwiGLU) map: fixed point q = 1 -> {:.6f}, slope there {:.4f}.\n", gated(1.0), (gated(1 + e) - gated(1 - e)) / (2 * e));
  for (double q0 : {sg * 0.0733, 1.1, 0.9}) {
    double q = q0;
    std::print("  from q = {:.3f}:", q0);
    for (int l = 0; l < 9 && q < 1e12; ++l) { q = gated(q); std::print(" {:.3g}", q); }
    std::print("\n");
  }

  // Depth: 30 bias-free layers of width 256 with LeCun-normal weights, measured against mean field.
  constexpr int depth = 30, width = 256, batch = 256;
  const std::vector<std::int64_t> widths(depth + 1, width);
  const std::vector<std::pair<Activation, dm::graphics::RGB>> acts = {
      {Activation::Selu, {220, 38, 38}}, {Activation::Elu, {22, 163, 74}}, {Activation::Tanh, {234, 88, 12}}, {Activation::Relu, {37, 99, 235}}};
  auto pf = dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), pb = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  std::vector<double> layers;
  for (int l = 1; l <= depth; ++l) layers.push_back(l);
  std::print("\n| activation | measured RMS z₁₀ | mean field | measured RMS z₃₀ | mean field | measured grad RMS at layer 1 | mean field |\n| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for (const auto& [a, col] : acts) {
    nn::Generator gen(7);
    const auto sp = nn::init::signal_propagation(widths, nn::init::variance_scaling(1.0, nn::init::FanMode::FanIn, nn::init::Distribution::Normal),
                                                 [a](const nn::Tensor& z) { return nn::activate(z, a); }, batch, gen);
    // Mean field: q_1 = 1, q_{l+1} = E f(sqrt(q_l) Z)^2; gradient variance at layer l = prod_{k >= l} E f'(sqrt(q_k) Z)^2.
    std::vector<double> q{1.0}, d2;
    for (int l = 0; l < depth; ++l) {
      const auto m = nn::activation_moments(a, std::max(q.back(), 1e-300));
      d2.push_back(m.derivative_second_moment);
      if (l + 1 < depth) q.push_back(m.second_moment);
    }
    std::vector<double> back(depth);
    double acc = 1;
    for (int l = depth - 1; l >= 0; --l) back[l] = (acc *= d2[l]);
    std::vector<double> mf_f, mf_b, ms_f, ms_b;
    for (int l = 0; l < depth; ++l) {
      mf_f.push_back(0.5 * std::log10(q[l])), mf_b.push_back(0.5 * std::log10(back[l]));
      ms_f.push_back(std::log10(sp.forward_rms[l])), ms_b.push_back(std::log10(sp.backward_rms[l]));
    }
    std::print("| {} | {:.4f} | {:.4f} | {:.3g} | {:.3g} | {:.3g} | {:.3g} |\n", nn::activation_name(a), sp.forward_rms[9], std::sqrt(q[9]),
               sp.forward_rms[29], std::sqrt(q[29]), sp.backward_rms[0], std::sqrt(back[0]));
    pf.lines(layers, mf_f, nn::activation_name(a), col, 2.0).points(layers, ms_f, col, 3.0);
    pb.lines(layers, mf_b, nn::activation_name(a), col, 2.0).points(layers, ms_b, col, 3.0);
  }
  pf.x_limits(0, 31).y_limits(-5, 2).title("Forward: RMS of pre-activations").x_label("layer l").y_label("log10 RMS z_l");
  pb.x_limits(0, 31).y_limits(-5, 2).title("Backward: RMS of dL/dz_l").x_label("layer l").y_label("log10 RMS gradient");
  auto fig = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
  fig.add(pf).add(pb);
  fig.size(1100, 440).fit_panels();
  fig.save("build/activations_depth.svg");
}
```
